// Automated strategy selection, bounded side.
//
// The buffer never leaves `main`: no return, no callee, no external store. Its
// payload is plain data, the programmer wrote no release, and the byte count is
// computed rather than constant, so neither the stack promotion nor a hand
// written allocator applies. Automated selection therefore puts it in the
// activation's scratch arena, which is created at entry and destroyed on the way
// out.
//
// The emitted IR is the proof: one `nrq_cdmm_arena_allocate`, one create, one
// destroy, and no general-allocator call at all.
int function main() {
    var count = 4;
    var value = memory.allocate<int>(count * 8);
    value[0] = 10;
    value[1] = 20;
    value[2] = 30;
    value[3] = 40;
    print(value[0] + value[1] + value[2] + value[3]);
    return 0;
}
